y that have a + icon next to them will add it to the workspace on the right hand side.</span><br /></p><table style=\"border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:#cccccc;width:623px;height:62px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;\"><tbody><tr style=\"height:33.333333333333336%;\"><td style=\"width:35.7252%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:#cccccc;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjE1OTgwODMwMzIsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Discord</span></td><td style=\"width:64.2748%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:#cccccc;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjEyMDk0MjYxODIsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Allows the workflow to post a message to Discord.</span></td></tr><tr style=\"height:33.333333333333336%;\"><td style=\"width:35.7252%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:#cccccc;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjU2NDQwMTE4OSwiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">EventTrigger</span></td><td style=\"width:64.2748%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:#cccccc;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjU5Mzk3MzQ1LCJkYXRhVHlwZSI6InNjZW5lIn0K(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Allows the workflow to trigger an event, this could be kicking off a workflow to generate offers for example.</span></td></tr><tr style=\"height:33.333333333333336%;\"><td style=\"width:35.7252%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:#cccccc;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjYyMTM1OTI1NSwiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">FormSubmission</span></td><td style=\"width:64.2748%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:#cccccc;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjE1NDY5NzMyOTIsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Enables the workflow to submit a form which will create new rows in the database.</span></td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Discord</h3><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjYwMDA1ODc1NSwiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">When you click on the Discord section, this is how it is broken down:</span></p><p style=\"text-align:center;\"><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" width=\"289\" height=\"126\" /><br /></p><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjU5OTMwMTgwMCwiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">This table breaks down each of them further, allowing you to understand their purpose. Clicking on any that have a + icon next to them will add it to the workspace on the right hand side.</span></p><table style=\"border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:#cccccc;width:640px;height:58px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;\"><tbody><tr style=\"height:50%;\"><td style=\"width:40.7285%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:#cccccc;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjIwMTU2NTcxMzMsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Discord Send Attachment to Channel</span></td><td style=\"width:59.2715%;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjcyMzE5NDc0NywiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Enables the workflow to send a message with an attachment to a discord channel. </span></td></tr><tr style=\"height:50%;\"><td style=\"width:40.7285%;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjUyMDU2MTkxNiwiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Discord Send Message to Channel</span></td><td style=\"width:59.2715%;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjM4NjEwNTU1NiwiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Enables the workflow to send a message to a discord channel.</span></td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Core</h3><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjkxMDczNjYzNywiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">When you click on the Core section, this is how it is broken down:</span></p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" style=\"display:block;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;\" width=\"266\" height=\"162\" /></p><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjUwODEzNzM4MywiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">This table breaks down each of them further, allowing you to understand their purpose. Clicking on any that have a + icon next to them will add it to the workspace on the right hand side.</span></p><table style=\"border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:#cccccc;width:589px;height:131px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;\"><tbody><tr style=\"height:33.333333333333336%;\"><td style=\"width:43.6437%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:#cccccc;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjQ3NzI0MTQ5NCwiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">ExecuteFlow</span></td><td style=\"width:56.3563%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:#cccccc;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjcyOTQzNzUyMCwiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Enables the workflow to execute another workflow.</span></td></tr><tr style=\"height:33.333333333333336%;\"><td style=\"width:43.6437%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:#cccccc;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjUwNTcwNzQ0NCwiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">QueueBackgroundJob</span></td><td style=\"width:56.3563%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:#cccccc;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjM1ODg1MzU1MSwiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Allows the workflow to queue a process that will run in the background, one example is transactions import.</span></td></tr><tr style=\"height:33.333333333333336%;\"><td style=\"width:43.6437%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:#cccccc;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjExNTczOTcyLCJkYXRhVHlwZSI6InNjZW5lIn0K(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Start</span></td><td style=\"width:56.3563%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:#cccccc;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjE5MzM1MDUwMjMsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Allows the workflow to start a new workflow, for example automatically generating offers after transactions have been imported.</span></td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Generate Offer Params<br /></h3><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjE1OTE3Njc3OTIsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">When you click on the GenerateOfferParams section, this is how it is broken down:</span></p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" style=\"display:block;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;\" width=\"262\" height=\"79\" /></p><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjgxMDUxOTYyNiwiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">This table breaks down each of them further, allowing you to understand their purpose. Clicking on any that have a + icon next to them will add it to the workspace on the right hand side.</span></p><table style=\"border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:#cccccc;width:607px;height:13px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;\"><tbody><tr style=\"height:100%;\"><td style=\"width:50%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:#cccccc;text-align:center;\">GenerateOffers</td><td style=\"width:50%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:#cccccc;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjE0ODU2OTI0MjgsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Allows the workflow to generate offers in the system, taking into account the funding details in the system.</span></td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Templating</h3><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjE5OTQ0OTQ3NTEsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">When you click on the Templating section, this is how it is broken down:</span></p><p style=\"text-align:center;\"><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" width=\"259\" height=\"116\" /></p><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjUxODM3NzM5MSwiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">This table breaks down each of them further, allowing you to understand their purpose. Clicking on any that have a + icon next to them will add it to the workspace on the right hand side.</span></p><table style=\"width:607px;border-style:solid;margin-right:auto;margin-left:auto;height:13px;\"><tbody><tr style=\"height:65px;\"><td style=\"border-style:solid;width:303px;text-align:center;\">PageBuilder</td><td style=\"border-style:solid;width:303px;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjE0ODU2OTI0MjgsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjE4NjA1MTEwODMsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Allows the workflow to build out a page, based on the parameters given.</span></td></tr><tr style=\"height:65px;\"><td style=\"border-style:solid;width:303px;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjE3NjMxMzUzMzgsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">SendEmail</span></td><td style=\"border-style:solid;width:303px;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjE4NjQ0OTc4NjcsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Enables the workflow to send out an email, to the current user or a specified account, typically a support account.</span></td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Sftp<br /></h3><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjMyMDMxOTM2NywiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">When you click on the Sftp section, this is how it is broken down:</span></p><p style=\"text-align:center;\"><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" width=\"279\" height=\"257\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p><table style=\"width:607px;border-style:solid;margin-right:auto;margin-left:auto;height:134px;\"><tbody><tr style=\"height:65px;\"><td style=\"border-style:solid;width:303px;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjIwNDc2MDI1ODcsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">SftpCreateBinaryFiles</span></td><td style=\"border-style:solid;width:303px;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjE0ODU2OTI0MjgsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjEwNzM5MzQ2NjYsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Allows the workflow to create binary files on the SFTP server.</span></td></tr><tr style=\"height:25px;\"><td style=\"border-style:solid;width:303px;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjc1MDA0MzIxOCwiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">SftpCreateTextFiles</span></td><td style=\"border-style:solid;width:303px;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjE3NjgxOTg0MTksImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Allows the workflow to create text files on the SFTP server.</span></td></tr><tr style=\"height:25px;\"><td style=\"border-style:solid;width:303px;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjM0NjAzMTUwNywiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">SftpDelete</span></td><td style=\"border-style:solid;width:303px;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjE1MTQ2MzM4ODIsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Allows the workflow to delete a file or folder from the SFTP server.</span></td></tr><tr style=\"height:25px;\"><td style=\"border-style:solid;width:303px;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjE3MTI5NTc5NjUsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">SftpFetch</span></td><td style=\"border-style:solid;width:303px;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjE2MTkxODQ0NjIsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Allows the workflow to retrieve any necessary files/data it requires from the SFTP server</span></td></tr><tr style=\"height:25px;\"><td style=\"border-style:solid;width:303px;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjE2ODIzMzA3MTIsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">SftpMove</span></td><td style=\"border-style:solid;width:303px;text-align:center;\"><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjIwNjg2NzA3NjgsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Ensures the workflow can move files from one location to another on the SFTP server.</span></td></tr></tbody></table><h2><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Right-Hand Workspace</span></h2><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjc5MjE3NDc5NSwiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">This is where you can set up your workflow, the green lines attach tasks together and they define the order of events. For ease of use, the boxes that contain the tasks can be dragged around. This allows you to rearrange them and re-order them quite easily.</span></p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" width=\"1149\" height=\"674\" style=\"display:block;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;\" /></p><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjExMzMwNjQzODQsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">When you add things to your workflow from the left-hand menu, they will be added to the workspace on the right-hand side. Each and every thing on the left-hand menu is unique and will require its own unique configuration to work. This documentation covers a basic example of the different things that need configuring to ensure that they work. This is where in-depth knowledge of the technicalities of the CLeX platform is beneficial as it will allow you to understand how workflows work and their setup.</span></p><h3><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Green Connections</span></h3><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjExNDk4ODgwNzIsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">As briefly explained above, this is how you connect the events of a workflow to one another, of course, the results of one task need to be used by succeeding tasks within the workflow. The green dot in-between each task can be interacted with. When you click this green dot, it brings up a dialog that contains a code editor that looks something like this:</span></p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" width=\"746\" height=\"229\" style=\"display:block;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;\" /></p><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjM1NDkyOTk1LCJkYXRhVHlwZSI6InNjZW5lIn0K(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">This is the green dot from the screenshot that lies between the <strong>&ldquo;Queue Background Job&rdquo;</strong> task and the <strong>&ldquo;Move Processed Files&rdquo;</strong> tasks. The first thing defined, is the file&rsquo;s destination folder. When the files are moved from the received folder, they are moved to this location. The <strong>&ldquo;files&rdquo;</strong> variable gets all of the files from the received folder. The <strong>&ldquo;files.Add&rdquo;</strong> takes the files and transforms them to a json file and puts them into the <strong>&ldquo;transformed&rdquo;</strong> folder.  To confirm any changes you&rsquo;ve made in the dialog, you click the submit button in the dialog.</span></p><h3><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Edit Button</span></h3><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjk0NzYwMjM5LCJkYXRhVHlwZSI6InNjZW5lIn0K(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">This button is responsible for different things, depending on the task you wish the workflow to carry out. Clicking on the <strong>&ldquo;Edit&rdquo;</strong> button will bring up a dialog that looks something like this:</span><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjkzOTY0MzYxLCJkYXRhVHlwZSI6InNjZW5lIn0K(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span></p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" width=\"516\" height=\"469\" style=\"display:block;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;\" /></p><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjIwMTg3NzMzNDYsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">The <strong>&ldquo;Type&rdquo;</strong> determines where in the api the task is defined, the <strong>&ldquo;Ref&rdquo;</strong> is the reference to the task you wish to carry out. Here, you can define the &ldquo;Path&rdquo; as the path at which you want the file to be moved to. The <strong>&ldquo;AppId&rdquo;</strong> is the Id of the application you wish to move the files within. The <strong>&ldquo;AuthToken&rdquo;</strong> and the <strong>&ldquo;AuthToken&rdquo;</strong> are filled in by the system when the workflow is run. <strong>&ldquo;BaseUrl&rdquo;</strong> for example looks something like this &ldquo;demo.dev.corporatelinx.com/api&rdquo;, it just means the base url for the application&rsquo;s api. You can confirm these changes by clicking the submit button in the dialog.</span></p><h3><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">The Close Button</span></h3><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjEzNDA2NjQwMjYsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Each activity has a close button in the top right-hand corner, when this is clicked, it removes the activity from the workspace in the right hand side.</span></p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" style=\"display:block;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;\" width=\"232\" height=\"120\" /></p><h2>Left-Hand Toolbar</h2><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjEzMjM5NjA0MywiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">This is where the basic functions are for the workflow, <strong>&ldquo;Settings&rdquo;,</strong> <strong>&ldquo;Run&rdquo;</strong> and <strong>&ldquo;Save&rdquo;</strong>. </span></p><h3><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Settings</span></h3><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjE0MTc2MDY0NzAsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Clicking the <strong>&ldquo;Settings&rdquo;</strong> button brings up a dialog that looks something like this:</span><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjU1OTIwMTk3NywiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span></p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" style=\"display:block;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;\" width=\"346\" height=\"334\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjIwNjQzMDI4MjcsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">The settings here determine who in the system can run the workflows. Typically this is an <strong>administrator only</strong> process as a lot of the workflows are responsible for things like, processing transactions or generating offers. These tasks can <strong>only</strong> be carried out by admins.</span></p><h3><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Run</span></h3><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjMwNTQzNDE4MCwiZGF0YVR5cGUiOiJzY2VuZSJ9Cg==(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">This button can be used to run the workflow that you&rsquo;re currently looking at. Having this button here allows you to quickly run things once things have been adjusted or set up. It&rsquo;s also useful if there are any issues to debug as you don&rsquo;t need to venture to another part of the UI to run the workflow.</span></p><h3><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">Settings</span></h3><p><span data-metadata=\"<!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiZW1aN281RHZZWTVGdTZpZzZGTkFKZiIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjE0Nzg1MDA3NDksImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)-->\"></span><span data-buffer=\"<!--(figma)(/figma)-->\"></span><span style=\"white-space-collapse:preserve;\">This saves any changes you&rsquo;ve made in the right hand side workspace will be saved with this button, whether that&rsquo;s removing an activity or altering its settings. They will not be saved until this button is pressed.</span></p>"
    }
  ],
  "PageInfo": [
    {
      "CultureId": "",
      "Description": "Workflow Designer",
      "Keywords": "Workflow Designer",
      "Title": "Workflow Designer"
    }
  ]
}
"""
            },
            new PackageItem
            {
                Type = "Core/Page",
                Data = """
{
  "Path": "Documentation/SSODocumentation/Registration",
  "Name": "Registration",
  "ShowOnMenus": true,
  "Order": 0,
  "LastUpdated": "2024-08-22T12:04:13.153507+01:00",
  "Layout": "Documentation",
  "Contents": [
    {
      "CultureId": "",
      "Name": "body",
      "Html": "<h2>Registering to the Portal</h2><p>When you first access the portal you want to register, you'll be greeted with their login page. To register for an account for this portal you click the <strong>\"Register\" </strong>button which will bring up a dialog that looks something like this:</p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" width=\"791\" height=\"486\" style=\"display:block;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;\" /></p><p>The <strong>\"D</strong><strong>isplay Name\"</strong> here is the username you wish to sign in with, the <strong>\"E</strong><strong>mail\"</strong> address should be filled in with your company email address. The&nbsp;<strong>\"Password\" </strong>and the <strong>\"Confirm Password\" </strong>fields need to be filled in with the password you wish to use when signing into the portal. You&nbsp;<strong>must </strong>read and agree to the terms and conditions and the data protection policy to create an account with our portals. To view these documents, click the links and you will be redirected to the page where you can read them.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "PageInfo": [
    {
      "CultureId": "",
      "Description": "This page explains how to complete registration for a cCoder portal.",
      "Keywords": "Registration",
      "Title": "Registration"
    }
  ]
}
"""
            },
            new PackageItem
            {
                Type = "Core/Page",
                Data = """
{
  "Path": "Documentation/SSODocumentation/SSOAPI",
  "Name": "SSO API",
  "ShowOnMenus": true,
  "Order": 0,
  "LastUpdated": "2024-08-22T12:04:13.1674907+01:00",
  "Layout": "Documentation",
  "Contents": [
    {
      "CultureId": "",
      "Name": "body",
      "Html": "<h2>Our SSO API</h2><p>You can use our Single Sign On (SSO) API to perform different tasks, for example you can use it to register for an account, or use it to sign into an existing account in our system.<br /></p><p>When you register for an account in our portal, it does two things:</p><ul><li>Sets up an account in our SSO database,</li><li>Adds you as a user to the portal you're registering to (this essentially gives you very minimal access to the portal, further access has to be applied for).</li></ul><p>To understand more about our SSO API, you can view more details about the possible requests you can make in our <a href=\"[app[root]]Documentation/SSODocumentation/SSOAPI/SSOMetadata\">SSO Metadata grid</a>.</p><h2>Registering using our API</h2><p>The first thing you have to do is build out your registration request, this will look something like this:</p><p><span style=\"font-family:var(--bs-font-monospace);font-size:0.875em;color:var(--kendo-color-on-app-surface, #212529);font-weight:var(--bs-body-font-weight);text-align:var(--bs-body-text-align);\">HTTP POST </span><a href=\"https://%3Cappurl%3E/Api/Account/Login\">https://&lt;AppURL&gt;/Api/Account/Login</a></p><pre style=\"background-color:#ffffff;font-family:var(--bs-font-monospace);font-size:12px;\">        {\n            DisplayName: \"Joe Bloggs\",\n            Email:\"joe.bloggs@corporatelinx.com\",\n            Password:\"superSecretPassword123!!\",\n            Culture: \"en-GB\",\n            PhoneNumber: \"01234 567 890\",\n            AppId: 0\n        }</pre><p>AppId is an optional field (it doesn't matter if you don't have one, providing one will automatically register the account with in the app with that particular Id).</p><p>The rest of this information is standard information that you would expect to have to provide on any account creation.</p><h2>Logging in using our API</h2><p>You can now use the details you just set up to authenticate and get a token. This request will look something like this:</p><p><span style=\"font-family:var(--bs-font-monospace);font-size:0.875em;color:var(--kendo-color-on-app-surface, #212529);font-weight:var(--bs-body-font-weight);text-align:var(--bs-body-text-align);\">HTTP POST&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://%3Cappurl%3E/Api/Account/Register\">https://&lt;AppURL&gt;/Api/Account/Login</a><span style=\"font-family:var(--bs-font-monospace);font-size:0.875em;color:var(--kendo-color-on-app-surface, #212529);font-weight:var(--bs-body-font-weight);text-align:var(--bs-body-text-align);\"></span></p><pre style=\"background-color:#ffffff;font-family:var(--bs-font-monospace);font-size:12px;\">        {\n            User: &ldquo;joe.bloggs@corporatelinx.com&rdquo;,\n            Pass: &ldquo;superSecretPassword123!!\"\n        }</pre><p>When this request is made, the server responds with a token which can be used in all subsequent calls you make to the API.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "PageInfo": [
    {
      "CultureId": "",
      "Description": "SSO API",
      "Keywords": "SSO API",
      "Title": "SSO API"
    }
  ]
}
"""
            },
            new PackageItem
            {
                Type = "Core/Page",
                Data = """
